🚽 Test case: #206 (3e) -- an array field whose element type is a
🚽 struct/union (or enum) `lit` alias (`lit gang P PT; gang S { PT
🚽 arr[2]; };`) is rejected: arrays of aggregate elements aren't supported
🚽 yet, matching the primitive array-field rule (which never accepts a
🚽 struct_or_union element type). A pointer-element array via alias is a
🚽 different, already-supported path (lit_struct_pointer_alias_array).
gang P {
    rizz x;
};

lit gang P PT;

gang S {
    PT arr[2];
};

skibidi main {
    gang S s;
    yapping("unreached");
}
